            "key_investigations.5",
            "key_investigations.6",
            "treatment.0",
            "treatment.1",
            "treatment.2",
            "treatment.3"
          ],
          "text": "On admission (Day 1) he had a temperature of 37.6, RR 58, mild-moderate subcostal recession, widespread fine creps and wheeze, and sats of 90% on room air. He was alert and not clinically dehydrated but had reduced intake. NPA confirmed RSV. He was managed with supplemental O2 to maintain sats >=90% and NG feeds. No antibiotics were given (viral aetiology) and no salbutamol was given (not indicated in bronchiolitis). By Day 2 he had weaned off O2 overnight with sats 93–95% in air, RR 44, only mild recession, and was taking approximately 75% orally with the NG removed. By later on Day 2 he was tolerating full oral feeds with stable sats in air and minimal work of breathing, and was discharged.",
