          ],
          "text": "Your child came in because they had:\n- a runny nose\n- a worsening cough\n- noisy breathing\n- poor feeding\n- fewer wet nappies\n\nThe team found your child had bronchiolitis. This was confirmed by a nose and throat swab (nasopharyngeal aspirate), which showed RSV (a common virus that causes bronchiolitis)."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "When your child came in, their breathing was fast and they needed extra oxygen. A nose and throat swab was taken.\n\nThe team gave your child:\n- extra oxygen, to keep their oxygen levels up\n- feeds through a tube into their nose (a nasogastric tube), as they were not feeding well enough by mouth\n\nNo antibiotics were given, as this illness is caused by a virus. No salbutamol was given, as it is not used for bronchiolitis.\n\nOver the next day, your child's breathing improved. They came off the extra oxygen. Their feeding improved and the nose tube was removed. By day 2, your child was taking full feeds by mouth and their breathing was much easier."
        },
